-- Migration 0023: full policy texts for the three legal pages.
--
-- Content-only migration (no schema change). Replaces the short
-- starter texts seeded by 0020 with complete Privacy Policy,
-- Terms of Use and Accessibility pages written for Bodhisattva
-- International (structure reviewed with ChatGPT 2026-11-20;
-- every statement checked against what the website actually
-- does: accounts with email verification, Gift Shop with cash
-- on delivery only, contact form, essential cookies only, no
-- trackers, no card data).
--
-- Before each page is overwritten, its CURRENT content is
-- snapshotted into site_policy_revisions (saved_by NULL = system),
-- so the previous text stays in the page's History in the admin
-- and can be restored from there. Versions bump by one.

--> statement-breakpoint
INSERT INTO `site_policy_revisions` (`slug`, `title`, `body_html`, `version`, `saved_by`)
SELECT `slug`, `title`, `body_html`, `version`, NULL FROM `site_policies` WHERE `slug` = 'privacy-policy';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `site_policies` SET `body_html` = '<h2>Who we are</h2><p>Bodhisattva International operates this website for Bodhisattva Gallery and the Purna Museum of Newa Art, House No. 91, Diamond Marg, Kupondole, Lalitpur, Nepal. This Privacy Policy explains what personal information the website collects when you visit, register an account, place an order in the Gift Shop, or contact us — and what we do with it.</p><p>We collect only the information we need to run the website, manage accounts, deliver orders and answer enquiries. We do not sell personal information, and we do not use it for purposes unrelated to the reason it was collected.</p><h2>Information we collect</h2><p><strong>Account information.</strong> When you register, we collect your name, email address and phone number. We verify your email address by sending a one-time code to it. Your password is stored only as a secure cryptographic hash; nobody at Bodhisattva International can read it, and we never store passwords in readable form.</p><p><strong>Gift Shop orders.</strong> When you place an order, we collect the delivery recipient name, phone number and address, together with a record of the items ordered, the amounts charged and the invoice we issue. Payment is cash on delivery: <strong>we never collect or store credit-card, debit-card or bank-account details</strong>, because the website does not take payment.</p><p><strong>Contact form.</strong> When you send us a message through the contact form, we collect your name, email address, the subject you choose and your message, so that we can reply to you.</p><p><strong>Technical information.</strong> Our servers keep standard logs, such as IP address and browser type, which we use for security and troubleshooting. We do not use analytics services, advertising trackers or social-media pixels, and we do not build profiles of how individual visitors use the website.</p><h2>Cookies</h2><p>This website uses only the cookies it needs in order to work:</p><ul><li>A <strong>session cookie</strong>, which keeps you signed in while you use the website.</li><li>A <strong>security cookie</strong>, which protects forms against cross-site request forgery (CSRF).</li></ul><p>Display preferences, such as the light or dark theme, are remembered in your own browser''s local storage and stay on your device. Because our cookies are essential, the website cannot offer to switch them off individually; you can block cookies in your browser settings, but signing in and ordering will then not work.</p><h2>How we use your information</h2><ul><li>To create and manage your account, verify your email address and sign you in.</li><li>To receive, review, approve and deliver your Gift Shop orders, and to issue your invoice.</li><li>To contact you about an order, for example to confirm delivery details.</li><li>To respond to messages you send us through the contact form.</li><li>To keep the website secure, prevent misuse and fix technical problems.</li></ul><p>We use your information for the purposes it was collected for. If we ever needed to use it for a different purpose, we would ask you first.</p><h2>Emails we send</h2><p>We send transactional emails only: verification codes, order confirmations, order status updates and invoices. We do not send marketing newsletters or promotional emails, and registering an account never subscribes you to any mailing list.</p><h2>Sharing your information</h2><p>We share personal information only where it is needed to provide the service you asked for:</p><ul><li><strong>Delivery:</strong> the recipient name, phone number and address are shared with the person or service delivering your order, so that your parcel can reach you.</li><li><strong>Staff:</strong> authorised members of our team can see account and order information in order to do their work.</li><li><strong>Law:</strong> we may disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect the rights and safety of our visitors, customers and staff.</li></ul><p>We do not sell or rent personal information to anyone.</p><h2>How we protect your information</h2><p>Passwords are stored as secure hashes, account areas are protected by sign-in (with additional verification for staff accounts), and access to personal information is limited to authorised staff. We take reasonable technical and organisational care with the information we hold. No website or internet service can be guaranteed completely secure, so please use a strong password that you do not reuse elsewhere, and tell us promptly if you believe your account has been used without your permission.</p><h2>How long we keep information</h2><ul><li><strong>Account information</strong> is kept while your account is active. If you ask us to close your account, we delete or anonymise the information we no longer need.</li><li><strong>Order and invoice records</strong> are kept for the period required by Nepalese accounting and tax law, even after an account is closed, because the law requires us to keep proper business records.</li><li><strong>Contact messages</strong> are kept so that we can follow up with you and keep a record of our correspondence.</li><li><strong>Server logs</strong> are kept for a limited period for security and troubleshooting, then deleted in the normal course of operations.</li></ul><h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>You can see and update your account details, including your delivery addresses, at any time from your account pages. You may also contact us to:</p><ul><li>Ask what personal information we hold about you.</li><li>Correct information that is wrong or out of date.</li><li>Ask us to close your account and delete your personal information, except for records we are required by law to keep (such as invoices).</li></ul><p>We will respond to requests within a reasonable time, and we may ask you to verify your identity before acting on a request, so that we do not give your information to the wrong person.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>This website and its Gift Shop are intended for adults. If you are under 18, please use the website with the involvement of a parent or guardian. If you believe a child has registered an account without such involvement, please contact us and we will close it.</p><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>If we change this policy, the new version will be published on this page together with its update date. Significant changes to how we handle personal information will be highlighted on this page when they take effect.</p><h2>Contact us</h2><p>Questions about this policy or about your personal information are welcome:</p><p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@bodhisattvainternational.com">info@bodhisattvainternational.com</a><br>Phone: <a href="tel:+9779818882876">+977 981-8882876</a><br>Bodhisattva International, House No. 91, Diamond Marg, Kupondole, Lalitpur, Nepal</p>', `version` = `version` + 1, `updated_at` = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(3) WHERE `slug` = 'privacy-policy';
--> statement-breakpoint
INSERT INTO `site_policy_revisions` (`slug`, `title`, `body_html`, `version`, `saved_by`)
SELECT `slug`, `title`, `body_html`, `version`, NULL FROM `site_policies` WHERE `slug` = 'terms-of-use';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `site_policies` SET `body_html` = '<h2>About these terms</h2><p>These Terms of Use govern your use of this website, including the Gift Shop. By using the website you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the website. Separate terms on this page cover purchases from the Gift Shop; if you place an order, those purchase terms apply to your order as well.</p><h2>About Bodhisattva International</h2><p>Bodhisattva International presents Bodhisattva Gallery and the Purna Museum of Newa Art, House No. 91, Diamond Marg, Kupondole, Lalitpur, Nepal. The website shares information about the museum, the gallery, exhibitions, collections and foundation programmes, maintains a digital press archive, and offers a selection of items for sale through the Gift Shop.</p><h2>Website content</h2><p>We work to keep the information on this website — exhibition dates, opening hours, collection descriptions, programme details and Gift Shop listings — accurate and up to date. Details can change, however, and content may occasionally contain errors or be unavailable while the website is maintained. If something important to your visit or purchase looks wrong, please contact us and we will check it for you.</p><h2>Intellectual property</h2><p>The text, images, artwork reproductions and other material on this website belong to Bodhisattva International, to the artists who created the works, or to their respective owners, and are protected by copyright and other rights. You may view and share links to pages for personal, non-commercial purposes. You may not copy, reproduce, republish or use material from this website for commercial purposes without written permission from the rights holder.</p><h2>The digital press archive</h2><p>The press archive collects newspaper and magazine clippings about the gallery, the museum and their artists, and is provided for historical, cultural and research purposes. Copyright in the clippings remains with their original authors, publishers or other rights holders; making a clipping available in this archive does not transfer any rights and does not make it free to reproduce. If you would like to reuse material from the archive, please seek permission from the rights holder. If you believe material in the archive infringes your rights, please contact us and we will review it promptly.</p><h2>Your account</h2><p>Some parts of the website, including the Gift Shop, require a registered account. When you register you must provide accurate information and verify your email address. You are responsible for keeping your password confidential and for activity that takes place under your account. Please tell us promptly if you believe your account has been used without your permission. We may suspend or close an account that is used in breach of these terms.</p><h2>Acceptable use</h2><ul><li>Do not use this website for anything unlawful.</li><li>Do not try to break, bypass or test the security of the website, or to access areas or accounts that are not yours.</li><li>Do not submit misleading, harmful or infringing content through any form on the website.</li><li>Do not interfere with the website''s operation, for example by flooding it with automated requests.</li></ul><h2>Gift Shop: products and prices</h2><p>Gift Shop products are described on their product pages, with photographs and, where relevant, details such as materials, dimensions and condition. Many items are handmade or one of a kind, so small variations between a photograph and the item itself are natural; a photograph is never a reason for us to supply something materially different from what was described. Prices are shown in Nepalese Rupees (NPR). The delivery charge and VAT, where they apply, are shown at checkout before you confirm your order, so the total you will pay on delivery is always clear before you order.</p><h2>Gift Shop: placing and confirming an order</h2><p>To order, you must be signed in to your account. Placing an order is an offer to buy the items in it. You will receive an email acknowledging that we have received your order; that acknowledgement is not yet an acceptance. Our team then reviews every order: when your order is approved, we issue your invoice and send it to you by email, and that approval is the point at which your purchase is confirmed. If we cannot approve an order — for example because an item has sold out — we will contact you, and no payment will be due.</p><h2>Gift Shop: payment</h2><p>Payment is <strong>cash on delivery</strong> only. You pay the amount shown on your invoice when your order is delivered. The website never asks for, collects or stores card numbers, bank-account details or electronic-wallet credentials. Please do not send such details to us by email or through the contact form; we will never ask for them.</p><h2>Gift Shop: delivery</h2><p>We deliver to addresses within Nepal. After your order is approved we will contact you, if needed, to confirm the delivery details and timing. We remain responsible for your order until it reaches you, even when a delivery partner carries it on our behalf. If the recipient is not available when delivery is attempted, we will contact you to arrange another attempt. Delivery charges, where they apply, are shown at checkout and on your invoice.</p><h2>Gift Shop: cancellations</h2><p>You may cancel an order at any time before it is dispatched, by contacting us with your order number; because payment is made on delivery, no refund process is needed for a cancellation before dispatch. If an order has already been dispatched, please contact us and we will do our best to help.</p><h2>Gift Shop: returns, refunds and damaged items</h2><p>Please check your items when they are delivered. If an item arrives damaged, is defective, or is not the item described on its product page, contact us promptly — ideally within seven days of delivery — with your order number and, if you can, a photograph of the problem. We will put it right: by repairing or replacing the item where possible, or by refunding the amount you paid for it, including VAT, if a replacement is not available or you do not wish to accept one. Refunds for cash-on-delivery purchases are made in cash or by another method we agree with you. Nothing in this section limits any rights you have under Nepalese consumer law.</p><p>If you simply change your mind about a purchase, please contact us. Where an item is unused and in its original condition we will try to help, but we cannot promise to accept every change-of-mind return, and some items — such as one-of-a-kind artworks — cannot be restocked once sold.</p><h2>Artwork and authenticity</h2><p>Where a product page states details about an item — its maker or artist, materials, age or origin — those statements are part of that item''s description, and we stand behind them as described. We do not make blanket claims that every item in the Gift Shop is certified, antique or an original artwork; please rely on the description of the specific item you are buying, and contact us if you would like more information about a piece before ordering.</p><h2>Complaints</h2><p>If something has gone wrong with an order or with the website, please tell us through the contact form, by email or by phone, giving your order number if you have one. We record every complaint, acknowledge it, and work to resolve it as promptly as we can. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may also raise the matter with the consumer-protection authorities in Nepal.</p><h2>Our responsibility</h2><p>We are responsible for the services we provide through this website and will always act honestly and with reasonable care. Nothing in these terms removes or limits rights that cannot lawfully be removed — including your rights as a consumer under Nepalese law — or our responsibility for loss caused by our own fraud or deliberate wrongdoing. Subject to that, if the website is unavailable or contains an error, our responsibility is limited to correcting the problem as described in these terms.</p><h2>Governing law</h2><p>These terms are governed by the laws of Nepal. If a disagreement arises, we ask that you contact us first so that we can try to resolve it directly and amicably; if that is not possible, the courts of Nepal will have jurisdiction.</p><h2>Changes to these terms</h2><p>If we change these terms, the new version will be published on this page together with its update date. Changes apply from publication, and the terms in force when you placed an order continue to apply to that order. Continuing to use the website after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p><h2>Contact us</h2><p>Questions about these terms, an order, or a complaint:</p><p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@bodhisattvainternational.com">info@bodhisattvainternational.com</a><br>Phone: <a href="tel:+9779818882876">+977 981-8882876</a><br>Bodhisattva International, House No. 91, Diamond Marg, Kupondole, Lalitpur, Nepal</p>', `version` = `version` + 1, `updated_at` = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(3) WHERE `slug` = 'terms-of-use';
--> statement-breakpoint
INSERT INTO `site_policy_revisions` (`slug`, `title`, `body_html`, `version`, `saved_by`)
SELECT `slug`, `title`, `body_html`, `version`, NULL FROM `site_policies` WHERE `slug` = 'accessibility';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `site_policies` SET `body_html` = '<h2>Our commitment</h2><p>Bodhisattva International is committed to making its website as accessible and inclusive as possible. Our visitors come to us for cultural, historical and educational information, and they access it in different ways — with keyboards, screen readers, magnification, touch and voice. We aim for the website to be usable by people with diverse abilities and access requirements, and we treat accessibility as ongoing work, not a finished state.</p><h2>What this statement covers</h2><p>This statement covers the public website: the museum, gallery, exhibition, collection and foundation pages, the digital press archive, customer accounts and the Gift Shop. It is about the website only; it does not describe the physical accessibility of the gallery and museum premises, which you are welcome to ask us about before a visit.</p><h2>How we build for accessibility</h2><p>We use the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at Level AA as our guide when we build and improve pages. In practice, that means we work to provide:</p><ul><li>A clear page structure with headings in order, so content can be navigated with assistive technology.</li><li>Meaningful alternative text for images that carry information, including artwork images.</li><li>Controls — buttons, links, menus and forms — that can be reached and used with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus indicator.</li><li>Text that is readable against its background, in sizes that can be enlarged in the browser without losing content.</li><li>Forms with clear labels and error messages that explain how to fix a problem.</li><li>Layouts that adapt to phones and tablets as well as desktop screens, without hiding content.</li></ul><p>We describe here what we aim for and check as we build; we do not claim that every page already meets every guideline in full.</p><h2>Known limitations</h2><p><strong>The digital press archive.</strong> Many clippings in the archive are scans of historical newspapers and magazines. Scanned pages are images: they may have no selectable text, no reading order and no document structure, so screen readers may not be able to read them properly, and the text cannot be resized or reflowed. Where the archive shows text extracted from a scan, that text is produced automatically and can contain errors, especially with older typefaces and damaged pages. The original printed clipping is always the authoritative version.</p><p><strong>Older content.</strong> Some images published earlier in the website''s life may have incomplete alternative text, and some documents may not yet be fully structured. We improve these as we review and republish content.</p><h2>Getting information in another format</h2><p>If part of the website is difficult for you to use, please contact us and tell us what you were trying to reach. We will do our best to provide the information another way — for example by reading or summarising content for you, sending it by email, or helping you complete an order by phone. Where copyright in archive material belongs to its original publisher, alternative formats may be limited to what the law allows, but we will always try to help you reach the information itself.</p><h2>Tell us about a problem</h2><p>Feedback genuinely improves the website. If you meet a barrier — a button you cannot reach, an image without a description, text you cannot read — please let us know:</p><p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@bodhisattvainternational.com">info@bodhisattvainternational.com</a><br>Phone: <a href="tel:+9779818882876">+977 981-8882876</a></p><p>It helps to tell us the page address, what you were trying to do, and the device or assistive technology you were using. We will acknowledge your message and use it to guide our fixes.</p><h2>Reviewing this statement</h2><p>We review this statement as the website changes and as our accessibility work progresses, and the date at the top of this page shows when it was last updated. Accessibility improvements are part of every significant update we make to the website.</p>', `version` = `version` + 1, `updated_at` = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(3) WHERE `slug` = 'accessibility';
